scaffold.details:
Write NibKit/Package.swift verbatim from CONTRACTS.md Part B. For every feature module create the stub entry NibKit/Sources/<Module>/<Module>Feature.swift = `import NibContracts

public enum <Module>Feature: NibFeature {
    public static let id = "<key>"
    public static func register(_ app: NibApp) {}
}` (key from the table in ARCHITECTURE.md §3) and the stub test NibKit/Tests/<Module>Tests/<Module>Tests.swift = `import XCTest
import NibContracts
import <Module>

@MainActor
final class <Module>Tests: XCTestCase {
    func testFeatureID() { XCTAssertFalse(<Module>Feature.id.isEmpty) }
}`. Split features add a second entry type in the SAME module (F101 FeatCanvasInputFeature, F102 FeatTextDocEditingFeature, F103 FeatTextDocExtrasFeature, F104 FeatSpellcheckFeature, F105 FeatRestyleFeature, F106 FeatMathAssistOverlayFeature, F107 FeatMathGraphFeature, F108 FeatCollabPresenceFeature, F109 FeatTeacherLessonsFeature, F110 FeatTeacherInsightsFeature): create the same stub entry file for each (`NibKit/Sources/<Module>/<EntryType>.swift`, key from ARCHITECTURE.md §3) and a stub test file for each at the first test path the spec lists for it, with the XCTestCase class named after the file (e.g. CanvasInputTests) so classes in one test target never collide. Also create the stub tests NibKit/Tests/ExamplePluginsTests/ExamplePluginsTests.swift and NibKit/Tests/IntegrationTests/IntegrationTests.swift (same shape, no module import) so every declared target has a source, and the placeholder resources Package.swift declares: NibKit/Sources/NibPluginRuntime/Resources/prelude.js (`// prelude placeholder`) and NibKit/Tests/NibAIProvidersTests/Fixtures/README.md. Features own and overwrite these stubs. Also create the reserved design module NibDesign (ARCHITECTURE.md §3): NibKit/Sources/NibDesign/NibDesign.swift = `public enum NibDesign {
    public static let version = 0
}` and an empty NibKit/Sources/NibDesign/Shaders/ kept by .gitkeep; Package.swift makes every ui/fullstack module depend on it.
